# Participant Sovereignty — MapAble Cursor Rule

Before proposing or editing features, read:

- `docs/product/MySupports-docs.md`
- `docs/development/FEATURE-DEVELOPMENT-MEMORY.md`
- `AGENTS.md`

Treat participant choice, AAC, informed consent, accessible refusal, correction, recovery, accountability and human alternatives as product requirements. Protect participant authority against provider-centred assumptions and automated overrides.

Use the current canonical repo and existing authorisation/data sources. Never call a suggested worker verified without evidence; never equate an AI proposal with an executed change; never describe synthetic or gated content as live.

Document and test normal, refused, cancelled, disputed, revoked-consent, cross-role, low-connectivity and AAC-mismatch scenarios. Keep sensitive features gated and fail closed. Never make production configuration, release, payment, booking, consent or schema changes without the proper separately approved scope and release gates.

At each substantial PR: update the feature dossier and the durable feature memory register, including actual CI status, outstanding accessibility/privacy reviews, deployment evidence and unresolved uncertainties. Do not put participant personal data or secrets in public markdown.
